# Unattended ops (FINAL)

When verifying git/HTTP/version/UI in Sotong24Work or SotongwareControl:

1. Prefer `scripts/cursor_safe/*` helpers over complex inline Python/PowerShell.
2. SAFE (no user Run): read git, analyze/test/build, explicit `git add` related files, `git commit`, HTTP GET/HEAD via helpers.
3. Always stop for user approval: `git push`, `deploy_control.ps1`, `firebase deploy`, `Remove-Item`, `git stash/reset/clean/checkout --/restore`, secrets, SotongwareWeb writes, Golden Run / STEP15 / STEP18 / START_JOB / new WI.
4. Never use `git add .` or `git add -A` when unrelated dirty files may exist — add related paths only.
5. Do not stash/reset/clean unrelated dirty WIP.
